            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Bouncebin 1.0.4</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Nothing to install any more.</b> Bouncebin carries its own copy of
      Python, so it runs on a Mac straight out of the disk image. ffmpeg is no
      longer needed either: without it, wav and aiff bounces are converted
      using the encoder built into macOS.</li>
  <li>The app always runs its own server now. It used to attach to one that
      was already running, which quietly meant showing you a different version
      of Bouncebin than the one you installed.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
